Derived from Needle, with modifications:

  - The Chrome extension (background.js, content.js, options.*, text-range.js)
    and its icons come from Needle. Identifiers, default server URL, messaging
    and copy were changed, and text-range.js now locates a sentence by its text
    when the server offset does not match the live page.
  - The backend was replaced. Needle calls the hosted Jev model through Vercel
    AI Gateway from a Node server. laya-needle calls Laya
    (https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya) in-process from Python, on the
    user's own machine. Node, React, Vite and the Vercel functions were removed.
  - Passage scoring was restructured. Needle scores every passage in one request.
    Laya reads at most 512-1024 tokens, so each passage is scored in its own
    forward pass.

Laya is created by Nandakishor M of Convai Innovations and is licensed under the
Apache License 2.0. This repository does not contain the model; it installs the
`laya` package and downloads the open weights from Hugging Face.
